In early chamber experiments, an initial warm-up period was identified for the NGM2611-E13 (Figure 6). In normal operation, a linear relationship is observed between the sensor output voltage and the air temperature. For up to 4 h after being powered, the sensor output does not follow this trend, presumably because the heating element in the sensor takes time to reach thermal equilibrium with the surrounding air. To avoid disrupting the calibration data, this warm-up period was excluded from the calibration data for the experiments detailed later.
